{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1484965-homebrew-new-path-korifos","id":1484965,"title":"[Homebrew] New Path: Korifos","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-06-25T08:11:45-07:00","id":1484965,"title":"[Homebrew] New Path: Korifos","content":"<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1h_ENjOM0OFnnblVSvMpsSsOmJuqIizCwHMNvYKcF5z0/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Click here to see it.</b></a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-08T18:06:59-07:00","id":1486077,"title":"","content":"The initial text of the Mystery Play on adaptability made me think of Life. Perseverance, endurance, survival are things it excels at.<br /> <br /> The gears analogy had me jumping between Fate, Time and Matter. But the emphasis on chaos and self determination made me think of Fate. I think Forces does not come across the Olympia's description as strongly as Fate. The lessened power of Space could be implied in a few more parts of the descriptions.<br /> <br /> Its a bit confusing that they think free will is non-verifiable, since Fate shows that Awakened will can tangle, reweave and rework the chain of causality to allow you to achieve your goals. By your own will, you forge an unprecedented path, even as you accept the struggles that come with that choice.<br /> <br /> A Korifos in the Seers seems odd, when their Mystery Play had them define themselves as the spanner in the works, revolting so completely against the system that they break it down with cataclysmic results.<br /> <br /> Since their element is water, wouldn't the Peng from Chinese mythology be a good symbol for the Path as well ? It transforms, endures (rather than be reborn like the phoenix), is strong and mighty in its momentum across the mountains and seas. <br /> <br /> I wonder if Earth would be more resonant as their element.They endure, are steady and reliable. Trope wise, they sem to be more the Determinator and Made of Iron, which both seem closer to that element.<br /> <br /> Overall they are very interested, capturing the feel of Guts struggling against those that twist causality, tempering himself in the crucible of war, forging a new path even as sparks ignite before his eyes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.t